    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "By default if no LSP completion available 'mini.completion' acts like user typed `<C-n>` to complete from sources defined in 'complete'. If it says `scanning tags`, it means that you have `t` in 'complete'. If you remove it with `set complete-=t`, this message won't show.\r\n\r\nBad news is, probably another message will be shown (something like \"Scanning \\<file\\>\"). I couldn't find the way to disable those messages. I hoped that having `c` in 'shortmess' would solve this but it is not the case. I think there is some issue or PR in Vim/Neovim to fix this, but don't quite remember. It was annoying for me at first, but then somehow I adapted to this.\r\n\r\nIf this is _really_ annoying, you can either disable fallback completion (supply `function() end` as `MiniCompletion.config.fallback_action`) or try something else (maybe other mapping from `:h ins-completion`).",
